menu "Powersuit node_helmet Configuration"

    choice PS_WAKE_ENGINE
        prompt "Wake-word / VOX engine"
        default PS_WAKE_ENERGY_GATE
        help
            Selects what decides when the mic uplink starts streaming
            (docs/safety.md §6). The energy-gate path is the default and must
            build without esp-sr present (it is not a default dependency,
            see main/idf_component.yml); esp-sr is an explicit opt-in for
            boards that have vendored it and populated the "model" partition
            (partitions.csv).

        config PS_WAKE_ENERGY_GATE
            bool "Energy gate (ps_egate, pure C, no model)"
            help
                RMS-over-window VOX gate from ps_audio: opens the uplink on
                any sound above threshold. No wake word, no model, always
                available.

        config PS_WAKE_ESP_SR
            bool "esp-sr wake word (WakeNet)"
            help
                NOT IMPLEMENTED. The option and the reserved "model" flash
                partition exist, but no WakeNet integration has been written.
                Selecting this fails the build with an #error explaining what
                is missing, rather than quietly falling back to the energy
                gate. Implementing it means adding espressif/esp-sr to
                main/idf_component.yml, flashing a model into the "model"
                partition, and feeding AFE/WakeNet from audio_in_task.c.
    endchoice

endmenu
